## §4.2 正文（直接粘 Overleaf）

```latex
\subsection{End-to-End Results}
\label{sec:e2e}

Table~\ref{tab:e2e} reports end-to-end execution time under revm and under
MHOT for the five workloads of Section~\ref{sec:setup}. MHOT is faster on every
workload, from $2.22\times$ on \texttt{nft-mint} to $3.84\times$ on
\texttt{erc20-heavy}, with a geometric mean speedup of $2.82\times$. We
aggregate per-workload speedups geometrically rather than averaging raw
execution times, so that the longest-running workload cannot set the aggregate
by itself.

The margin does not track how much work the baseline performs.
\texttt{erc20-heavy} attains the largest speedup in the suite from a baseline of
$287.3$\,ms, while \texttt{proxy-chain}, whose baseline is longer at
$344.0$\,ms, attains $2.30\times$; the two longest baselines,
\texttt{defi-mixed} ($523.8$\,ms) and \texttt{uniswap-v3} ($412.6$\,ms), land
close together at $3.06\times$ and $2.97\times$. The determining factor is the
composition of the executed bytecode rather than its volume.
% TODO(机理·一句): erc20-heavy 为什么最高？(比如某类 opcode/存储访问模式占比)

\texttt{nft-mint} is the least favourable workload in the suite, at
$196.1$\,ms under revm against $88.5$\,ms under MHOT ($2.22\times$).
% TODO(机理·一句): nft-mint 为什么最低？
Even there MHOT runs the workload more than twice as fast, and the geometric
mean above is taken over all five workloads.
